{#
settings/_calendar_sources.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Where mirrored calendars come from: the mail accounts whose provider carries
calendars on the grant they already hold, and the CalDAV servers connected for
calendars alone.

One list, because to a person they are the same thing — somewhere calendars
come from — and the difference only shows in what connecting one costs. A mail
account is here because it already signed in; a CalDAV server is here because
somebody typed its address.

The note at the bottom is not decoration. It is the answer to the question this
screen exists to answer: "I connected the account and no calendars appeared."
There are exactly three reasons, and a user cannot tell them apart without
being told what they are — a scope they unticked on Google's consent screen, a
permission their administrator has not added to the app registration (which is
what templates/admin/integrations/_mail_form.html.twig tells the admin about),
or an account that genuinely has no calendars.

Variables:
  calendarAccounts     Account[]      accounts with a calendar service behind them
  calendarConnections  Integration[]  CalDAV and anything else of ServiceKind::Calendar
#}
{% set has_sources = calendarAccounts is not empty or calendarConnections is not empty %}

<div class="px-4 py-3 border-b border-line bg-sunken space-y-2.5">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft">{{ 'settings.calendars.sources.heading'|trans }}</p>

        <button
            type="button"
            data-controller="ui--modal"
            data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
            data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'settings.calendars.caldav.title'|trans }}"
            data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_caldav_connect') }}"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 h-8 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium
                   text-ink-soft bg-field border border-field hover:bg-hover transition-colors cursor-pointer"
        >
            <i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-days text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{ 'settings.calendars.caldav.connect'|trans }}
        </button>
    </div>

    {% if has_sources %}
        <ul class="space-y-1.5">
            {% for account in calendarAccounts %}
                <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
                    <i class="fa-regular fa-envelope w-4 text-center text-xs text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="flex-1 min-w-0 truncate text-xs text-ink">{{ account.displayAddress }}</span>

                    <button
                        type="button"
                        data-controller="ui--modal"
                        data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
                        data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'settings.calendars.subscribe.title'|trans }}"
                        data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_subscribe', { kind: 'account', id: account.id }) }}"
                        class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 h-7 rounded-lg text-[11px] font-medium
                               text-accent hover:bg-hover transition-colors cursor-pointer"
                    >
                        {{ 'settings.calendars.sources.find'|trans({ '%name%': account.displayAddress }) }}
                    </button>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}

            {% for connection in calendarConnections %}
                <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
                    <i class="{{ connection.provider.icon }} w-4 text-center text-xs text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="flex-1 min-w-0 truncate text-xs text-ink">{{ connection.name }}</span>

                    {# The connection's own last failure, not a calendar's: a
                       server that stopped answering explains an empty list far
                       better than the empty list does. #}
                    {% if not connection.isHealthy %}
                        <span class="shrink-0 text-[11px] text-danger truncate max-w-[16rem]"
                              title="{{ connection.lastError }}">{{ connection.lastError }}</span>
                    {% endif %}

                    <button
                        type="button"
                        data-controller="ui--modal"
                        data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
                        data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'settings.calendars.subscribe.title'|trans }}"
                        data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_subscribe', { kind: 'integration', id: connection.id }) }}"
                        class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 h-7 rounded-lg text-[11px] font-medium
                               text-accent hover:bg-hover transition-colors cursor-pointer"
                    >
                        {{ 'settings.calendars.sources.find'|trans({ '%name%': connection.name }) }}
                    </button>

                    {# The confirmation names the connection and says the
                       mirrored calendars go with it, because they do — and
                       what only exists here moves rather than going with
                       them, which is the same promise the untick makes. #}
                    <form method="post"
                          action="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_caldav_disconnect', { id: connection.id }) }}"
                          data-turbo-confirm="{{ 'settings.calendars.caldav.disconnect_confirm'|trans({ '%name%': connection.name }) }}">
                        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar-disconnect' ~ connection.id) }}">
                        <button
                            type="submit"
                            class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-zinc-400 hover:text-danger hover:bg-danger-soft transition-colors cursor-pointer"
                            aria-label="{{ 'settings.calendars.caldav.disconnect'|trans({ '%name%': connection.name }) }}"
                            title="{{ 'settings.calendars.caldav.disconnect_title'|trans }}"
                        >
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-link-slash text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </button>
                    </form>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    {% else %}
        <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint italic">{{ 'settings.calendars.sources.empty'|trans }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    <details class="group/why">
        <summary class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint cursor-pointer select-none hover:text-ink-muted transition-colors">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-question mr-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{ 'settings.calendars.sources.why_empty'|trans }}
        </summary>
        <ul class="mt-1.5 ml-4 space-y-1 list-disc list-outside text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">
            <li>{{ 'settings.calendars.sources.why_consent'|trans }}</li>
            <li>{{ 'settings.calendars.sources.why_admin'|trans }}</li>
            <li>{{ 'settings.calendars.sources.why_none'|trans }}</li>
        </ul>
    </details>
</div>
